title Silence and cleanliness read alike, and the pin arrived past its bound with a wall standing
prompt the standing baton -- take the next agent-doable lap in the auditing lane, reds first
rota lap N 4101, N mod 5 = 1, which the last two laps on this pier already read; advanced by hand to row 2, FIRE -- Mars, cut and stop; threshold fire-the-row-that-sees, then standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal
think The fire row asks what must stop and what must be cut, so I opened on the sibling find my own last lap named and declined -- two shipped comment meters carrying the identical blindness I had just repaired in a third. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, and this one had fired twice already.
think I proved the blindness before believing my own note. Both scans run their counting awk as n=$(LC_ALL=C awk ... 2>/dev/null) and then [ -z "$n" ] && n=0, so awk's status is never examined and its complaint is discarded. Both meters sat AT their ceilings -- shell 505 of 505, Rye 3,793 of 3,794 -- which is exactly where a silent zero reads as the largest sweep the meter ever recorded.
obs MY FIRST PLANT PROVED THE WRONG MECHANISM AND I CAUGHT IT ON THE SECOND RUN. I inserted a comment between a trailing || and the newline continuing the statement -- the exact shape that broke my own document scan -- and read files=0 chars=0 as an awk refusal. GNU Awk 5.4.1 accepts that program: line = $0 || 0 makes line a boolean, so no line begins with # and the meter honestly counts nothing. Same symptom, different cause. The plant that actually proves the leg is an unclosed if (, a syntax error in every dialect. I would have shipped a control that tested nothing.
obs The real exit statuses were there the whole time: 1 on a syntax error, 2 on a file it cannot open. The scan never asked.
think The repair is a status read rather than a wider gate. The awk moves into count_file() whose exit status the caller examines, and three answers are told apart rather than collapsed -- absent is skipped and COUNTED and never fatal, because git ls-files reads the index and a rename staged mid-rebase is ordinary; refused is fatal and names the path; a non-numeric answer is refused too, since END { print n + 0 } prints a number whenever the program runs at all.
obs Every leg is proven from BOTH sides against the elder scans themselves, restored out of HEAD into a pen and read by the very same controls. Against the repaired files each leg reads the good answer; against the pre-repair files broken_instrument_named=no, broken_instrument_refuses=no (a perfect under_ceiling=yes over 3,159 files never opened), unreadable_verdict=no, absent_counted=no. A refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass.
obs The unreadable leg PROBES rather than assumes. chmod 000 is toothless for a privileged reader, so where the block does not bite the control says so by name and passes -- a control that reds on an environment it cannot test is a control somebody turns off, which is %493's own lesson from my last lap.
obs Readings unmoved by the repair, which is the whole point: shell files=153 chars=505 opened=3159, Rye files=313 chars=3793 opened=1717. The meters now also print instrument=ok and their reach, and the witness asserts instrument=ok on each living reading -- the one line that tells a meter which opened nothing from a meter which opened everything.
obs THEN THE SECOND FINDING FOUND ME, WHICH IS WHAT THE FIRE ROW IS FOR. Booking %513 meant touching construction/REDS.md, and the pin was already 41,153 bytes against the 40,960 its own header declares -- 193 over, before I changed a byte. Two witnesses were refusing on it and one of them, equinox_e123_living_pin_guard, is ROSTERED.
think The mechanism is not a missing wall but a wall on a path the work does not take. Rule three of tools/hooks/pre-commit refuses a commit staging an over-bound pin, reading the size off the index. It runs at git commit and git commit --amend and nowhere else. post-commit repairs that skip for RULE ONE by recording a page debt the next pre-commit pays, and records nothing at all for rule three. On an eight-ship fleet the twice-pulled send rebases whenever the anointed order moved, which today was most sends.
obs Proven in a pen with a hook that only records that it ran: four commits -- base, plain, side, amend -- produced exactly four entries, and the git rebase replaying the side commit produced none. The hook's own header says as much in words; what nothing said is that rule one's repair was never extended to rule three.
obs Measured so the class is not one bad night: of the last 120 commits touching construction/REDS.md, SIX shipped it over the bound its header declared at that commit. Both of today's carry a committer time later than their author time, the signature of a replay.
obs I repaired the instance and sized the class without taking it. %487 and %489 folded oldest-first, exactly as the ledger scan's own detail line prescribes; the pin reads 38,498 with 2,462 of headroom and both witnesses are GREEN. The class repair -- post-commit records a pin debt as it records a page debt -- is left for its own lap because eight ships run that file and a mistake in it is a fleet that cannot commit. That is %499's and %512's reason, and it is mine.
obs Folding one row would have left 363 bytes of headroom. I folded a second, because a repair that leaves the next hand one step from the fault has moved the fault rather than fixed it -- which is the same sentence as the finding.
obs The report card pushed one frame and I worked it down rather than around. The two controls read 60 and 63, both below B. Measured at molt time against HEAD: the shell control read 60 THERE TOO, so it is pre-existing and became a card line; the Rye control fell 73 to 63 on my own edit, so that one was my frame. Trimmed my four added header lines to short plain sentences: reach 0 to 30, composite 63 to 71.
obs THE FRAME CLOSES WITH A NUMBER RATHER THAN A REWRITE. The remaining two points against HEAD's 73 are 30 words of true new documentation about three new behaviors, against a Door reading-grade budget of 9 that this card already carries as an open question -- 115 of 163 sampled program heads read below B. Shrinking honest documentation until a contested ceiling is satisfied would be serving the meter rather than the reader.
obs The card had NINE bytes free when I arrived, so my account could not land at any honest length. What I folded is three lines whose entire content was this account is on a shelf, merged into one; the row list the first recited went with it because each shelf names its own rows in its own header. No peer's live prose was read or condensed, which the 113014 cairn rules is the move a cairn exists to refuse. Cairn written before the merge, not after.
obs And the card came back to 40,957 of 40,960 -- three bytes free -- so the next ship meets exactly the condition I did. That is %514's shape one room over and I left it standing rather than paying for it out of a peer's open account.
obs An erratum of my own hand: proving a leg I ran git stash push on the very file holding my repair, and stashed my own work mid-lap. Popped it back in the next breath, nothing lost. The dead-letter box exists because that move is easy to make.
obs THE HOT PASS CAME BACK WITH TWO REDS AND NEITHER IS THIS LAP'S. 153 guards, 148 green, 2 red, 3 gated, 991s, tree_moved=no. stash_record reads records_unlanded because two session logs stamped 20260906.162759 and 20260906.173013 stand in stash@{0} and on refs/heads/pier/diverged-20260906-210007 -- a park my OWN round-open made at 21:00:07, before this lap read a file. standing_equipment reds because it reads the run card and sees that one. The round-open announced both at the open, so the state predates every byte I wrote.
obs I am naming it rather than reaching for it, and the reason is the shape of the work. The parked commit 75a3a2778 is this tree's own prior lap -- a witness, a control and two logs -- pushed to xy by name and losing nothing. Recovering a package is a lap, not a coda, and folding someone's whole round into this commit would put two rounds' work under one mechanism sentence. It is %499's own subject: a park keeps every byte and still costs the lap.
